// @description sbp_WhooshEngine
// @version 4.01
// @author SBP & AI
// @changelog
//  v4.01 (2026-08-12):
//  Fixed transparent External Input routing and Filter bypass.
//  Audio Pitch and Physical Doppler bypass the granular reader at 0 semitones.
//  Added +12 dB External mixer makeup range.
//  v4.0 (2026-08-12) — Release summary:
//  Reworked synthesis, spatial workflow and FX stability for ReaWhoosh UI 2.0.
//  Hit Engine adds metallic Crash, shared Tone/Drive character and correct Chopper/Panning bypass routing.
//  Reverb routing, Chopper anti-click behavior, oscillator FM and extended generator controls are finalized.
//  All existing automation indices are preserved; new controls are append-only.
//  v3.8.3 (2026-08-11):
//  Added a sample-rate-independent anti-click ramp to Chopper; Hard mode now has a 1.5 ms minimum fade.
//  v3.8.2 (2026-08-11):
//  Fixed Hit transient and ducking to respect audible component levels; zeroed controls now produce no residual Hit sound.
//  v3.8.1 (2026-08-11):
//  Hit onset is now clickless; Crack is short, band-limited and lower in the default mix.
//  v3.8.0 (2026-08-11):
//  Added automation-triggered Hit Engine with transient, body, sub, crack, decay, tone, drive and ducking.
//  Hit activity keeps DSP and reverb tails alive after the Rise MIDI note ends at impact.
//  v3.6.1 (2026-08-11):
//  Unified Full Circles coordinates with the speaker view (0 degrees = Center/front).
//  Rotation now follows C-L-Ls-Rs-R-C for CCW and the reverse order for CW.
//  v3.6.0 (2026-08-11):
//  Unified the main amplitude envelope across Noise/Osc/Chua/External sources.
//  Sub now follows the main envelope exactly once, with MIDI gate used only for click-safe note release.
//  Full Circles rotation count now follows the real effect duration supplied by ReaWhoosh.
//  Added a bounded soft output limiter and kept all existing slider indices stable.

//  v3.5.7 (2026-02-20):
//  Reverb moved to true post-envelope behavior (tail keeps processing after amp envelope drops)
//  Removed final L/R gate clamp to prevent abrupt reverb cutoff
//  v3.5.6 (2026-02-20):
//  Smoothed post-FX envelope release to avoid abrupt reverb cutoff
//  Output gate release now follows Verb Tail for more natural fade-out
//  v3.5.5 (2026-02-20):
//  Reverb pre-delay slightly shortened for closer early tail response
//  v3.5.4 (2026-02-20):
//  Reverb comb-filter artifacts reduced: added internal diffusion all-pass stages
//  Added subtle delay-time modulation in reverb tank for smoother tail
//  v3.5.3 (2026-02-20):
//  Reverb moved to post-filter stereo stage (no new sliders)
//  Reverb now processes L/R independently with subtle decorrelated tails
//  v3.5.2 (2026-02-19):
//  Added Full Circles mode for unlimited rotations using internal phase accumulator
//  Surround modes now: Vector 3-point / Circle Arc 3-point / Full Circles
//  Removed Speed multiplier from Circle Arc mode (3-point automation defines timing)
//  Added Rotations Count & Start Angle parameters for Full Circles mode
//  Fixed proper VBAP 5.1 panning with mono source distribution
//  v3.5.1:
//  Fixed Surround Circle mode: removed broken play_position calculation, now uses sur_path_x/y automation
//  Implemented proper VBAP panning algorithm for ITU-R BS.775 5.1 layout
//  Fixed speaker position gaps causing audio dropouts during circular motion
//  v3.5.0:
//  Added dedicated Surround Path controls (Vector/Circle) with new automation sliders.
//  Surround output can now follow dedicated Sur Path X/Y stream from ReaWhoosh UI.
//  Ring Modulator has been enhanced.
//  v3.4.1:
//  Rename effect to "sbp_WhooshEngine" for better clarity and branding.
//  v3.4.0:
//  Added Physical Doppler Mode
//  Improved Audio Pitch algorithm for Doppler (Grain Jitter)
//  Added Grain Size selection for Audio Pitch/Doppler
//  Improved Pitch Logic (DC Blocking for low end)
// @link https://forum.cockos.com/showthread.php?t=305805
// @about effect core for SBP_ReaWhoosh.lua

desc: sbp_WhooshEngine v4.01
options:gmem=sbp_whoosh

